From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Connor McAdams <cmcadams@codeweavers.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Jan 2026 10:09:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] d3dx10: Add support for saving textures to non-DDS file
 formats.

Signed-off-by: Connor McAdams <cmcadams@codeweavers.com>

CW-Bug-Id: #20442
CW-Bug-Id: #23084
CW-Bug-Id: #23301
(cherry picked from commit df77a666b2bfc873f9b295ea1e6610364d564712)
mproton-resolved: The d3dx9 helper hunks (d3dx_save_pixels_to_memory() taking a destination format, WIC encoding moved to util.c) apply as is. The d3dx10 side is written on 11.20's helpers: a new d3dx10_save_texture_to_image_file() copies subresource 0 into a staging texture, maps it, and encodes it with d3dx_save_pixels_to_memory(); d3dx10_get_save_format_for_file_format() is Proton's. Test changes are left out (the save tests aren't carried).
